# Variables: `let`, `const`, and `var` 📦

Variables store data values in computer memory. Modern JavaScript provides three declaration keywords:

```javascript
let count = 10;
const appName = "QuizApp";
var legacyScore = 100;

count = 15; // Valid: let allows reassignment
// appName = "NewApp"; // TypeError: Assignment to constant variable!
console.log("Count:", count);
console.log("App:", appName);
```

