# The 7 Primitive Data Types 🏷️

JavaScript has 7 primitive data types stored directly on the stack:

| Primitive | Description | Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `number` | Integers and floats | `42`, `3.14159` |
| `string` | Text wrapped in quotes | `"Hello"`, `'World'`, `\`Hi\`` |
| `boolean` | Logical true or false | `true`, `false` |
| `undefined`| Variable declared but unassigned | `let x;` |
| `null` | Intentional absence of value | `let user = null;` |
| `symbol` | Unique immutable identifier | `Symbol("id")` |
| `bigint` | Arbitrary precision integers | `9007199254740991n` |

```javascript
let age = 25;
let username = "Alice";
let isActive = true;
console.log(typeof age, typeof username, typeof isActive);
```

