# Template Literals (`${...}`) 💬

Modern JavaScript uses backticks (`` ` ``) for template literals, allowing string interpolation and multi-line strings:

```javascript
let user = "Alice";
let points = 250;

// Old messy concatenation
let msg1 = "Welcome, " + user + "! You have " + points + " points.";

// Modern clean template literal
let msg2 = `Welcome, ${user}! You have ${points} points.`;
console.log(msg2);
```

